# PHASE 3 – PROJECT DESIGN

## 1. Introduction

The Project Design Phase defines the structure and workflow of the Employee Data Import and Management System.

The design explains how employee data moves from the Excel spreadsheet to the target employee table.

## 2. System Architecture

The project follows this basic architecture:

```text
Excel Spreadsheet
       ↓
Import Data
       ↓
Import Set Table
       ↓
Transform Map
       ↓
Field Mapping
       ↓
Transform Data
       ↓
Employee Test Table
       ↓
Employee Records
```

## 3. Data Flow

The employee data starts from the Excel spreadsheet.

The spreadsheet is uploaded into ServiceNow through the data import process. The data is temporarily stored in an Import Set table. A Transform Map is then used to map the source fields to the target fields.

After transformation, the employee records are stored in the Employee Test table.

## 4. Source Fields

The source spreadsheet contains:

* Employee ID
* Employee Name
* Department
* Email
* Location

## 5. Target Fields

The target Employee Test table contains corresponding fields:

* Employee ID
* Employee Name
* Department
* Email
* Location

## 6. Field Mapping

| Source Field  | Target Field  |
| ------------- | ------------- |
| Employee ID   | Employee ID   |
| Employee Name | Employee Name |
| Department    | Department    |
| Email         | Email         |
| Location      | Location      |

## 7. Workflow Design

```text
Start
  ↓
Prepare Excel File
  ↓
Load Data
  ↓
Create Import Set
  ↓
Create/Select Transform Map
  ↓
Map Fields
  ↓
Transform
  ↓
Verify Records
  ↓
Test
  ↓
End
```

## 8. User Interface Design

The project uses ServiceNow forms and list views for managing employee records.

The user can view employee records in a table format.

## 9. Database Design

The Employee Test table is used to store employee information.

